// core:script — what an untried call does when its script fails: the
// per-VM failure policy `#script_vm(…, on_error: …)` sets.
//
// Calls from Dado into a script — a member call `c.hit(3)`, a field read or
// written through a handle, `#script_new` — are not failable unless written
// under `try`. When one written without `try` fails, its text has already
// gone to the VM's error sink, and the policy decides what follows
// (`#script_run(c)` is the exception: it answers a status, as `main` exits
// with one, under either policy):
//
// * `QUIT`, the default: the program ends with the failure's status, after
//   one line on the error sink naming the method that failed.
// * `CONTINUE`: the call answers its type's zero value — `#script_new` a
//   handle that holds no script — and the program goes on, after one line
//   saying so.
//
// `try` is available either way, where the program wants the code. A stop is
// never a failure here: it answers the zero value under either policy.
package script

// The program ends with the failure's status.
const i32 QUIT = 0
// The call answers its type's zero value, and the program goes on.
const i32 CONTINUE = 1

private @thread_local i32 g_policy_next
private @thread_local bool g_policy_given

// The next VM's policy, `on_error:`.
void pend_policy(i32 policy):
    g_policy_next = policy
    g_policy_given = true

// The waiting policy, made the engine's for its life; `QUIT` when none was
// given.
private void take_policy(Engine e):
    e^.on_error = QUIT
    if g_policy_given && g_policy_next == CONTINUE:
        e^.on_error = CONTINUE
    g_policy_given = false

private void drop_policy():
    g_policy_given = false

// An untried call through `s` failed with `code`, not a stop: its last line
// on the error sink, and whether the program goes on — the handle's policy
// says, and a handle that holds no script has none, so it quits.
private bool goes_on(rawptr s, cstring entry, cstring verb, i32 code):
    Slot at
    if !slot_read(s, &at) || at.on_error != CONTINUE:
        untried(s, entry, verb, code)
        return false
    Sink err = failure_sink()
    failed_member(err, s, entry, verb)
    _ = io_write(err, "; its VM was made with `on_error: script.CONTINUE`, so it answers its zero value and the program goes on\n")
    return true
